  message: "FIXED (re-scoped) in GitHub PR #13 (dev 2e5ccab0ba). Actionable residual: the create_file_symbols inline path (base.py) minted kind=file nodes with a degenerate Span(1,0,1,0), so their whitespace-invariant structural fingerprint hashed only line 1 (shebang/comment -> filtered empty -> needless null) for ~13 tree-sitter analyzers (haskell/elm/dart/ocaml/...). Now spans the parsed extent (tree.root_node.end_point[0]+1), matching bash.py/js_ts.py + the synthesis paths. Identity-safe: make_file_id hardcodes :1-1: and make_file_stable_id hashes only (language,path) -> no id/stable_id churn (INV-sotiv/INV-vaguj). VERIFY-THE-PREMISE re-scope: the item's named bash/ts/go/rust/swift population already carried full-file spans; their ~6% nulls are cause-2 HONEST-NULLS from whole-file tree-sitter parse errors, SPEC-PERMITTED (spec §372 + spec_validator skips None) -> not a defect, policy-dissolved. Cause-1 (fingerprint.py ignoring grammar_module) MOOT at HEAD (bash resolves via the pack post-WI-givad); §372's stale 'bash has no grammar in the pack' clause corrected. 'Isolated bash function' facet = graph connectivity, orthogonal to fingerprint, not addressed. Evidence: new full-span test (end_point row 4 -> end_line 5); smart-test 10248 passed, 100% cov of changed files."  # db0a
